# 3. STANDARD SOD/EOD EMAIL FORMAT

All Start-of-Day (SOD) and End-of-Day (EOD) reports must follow a standardized, searchable format.

Do NOT use traditional email introductions such as:

- Greetings,
- Good morning,
- I hope you're doing well.
- Please see my report below.
- Any unnecessary opening or closing statements.

The report must begin immediately with the company name and reporting information.

## 3.1 Required Email Structure

**COMPANY NAME**

MMDDYYYY | START TIME - END TIME

**-START OF DAY REPORT-**

or

**-END OF DAY REPORT-**

## 3.2 Subject Line Format

Use this exact structure:

SOD:

`SOD - MMDDYYYY | COMPANY NAME`

EOD:

`EOD - MMDDYYYY | COMPANY NAME`

Examples:

`SOD - 11182026 | The Lynch Team`

`EOD - 11182026 | The Lynch Team`

The subject must always include:

- Report type: SOD or EOD
- Date in MMDDYYYY format
- Company name

## 3.3 SOD Report Structure

**[COMPANY NAME]**

[MMDDYYYY] | [START TIME] - [END TIME]

**-START OF DAY REPORT-**

**Planned Tasks:**
- List the day's planned tasks.
- Use clear, action-oriented descriptions.
- Identify important priorities and dependencies.

**Main Focus Areas:**
- Identify the primary objectives for the shift.

Rules:
- Include only planned or assigned tasks.
- Do not describe planned work as completed.
- Highlight important approvals, feedback, or information needed.
- Reflect the latest known task priorities.

## 3.4 EOD Report Structure

**[COMPANY NAME]**

[MMDDYYYY] | [START TIME] - [END TIME]

**-END OF DAY REPORT-**

**Tasks Completed:**
- List tasks actually completed.
- Describe specific deliverables and outcomes.
- Include relevant URLs as plain text.

**Huddle / Meeting Updates:**
- Include only when a meeting or meaningful coordination discussion occurred.
- Document decisions, instructions, priority changes, and action items.

**In Progress / Pending:**
- Identify unfinished work.
- Include pending approvals, feedback, dependencies, and blockers.

**Main Focus Areas:**
- Summarize the primary areas of work during the shift.

Do not include empty sections.

Do not report pending work as completed.

## 3.5 Report Formatting Rules

- Use the company name as the first line.
- Use MMDDYYYY date format.
- Use the agreed client time zone.
- Preserve the supplied shift time.
- Use bold section headings.
- Use concise bullet points.
- Preserve all supplied URLs as plain text.
- Do not include unnecessary greetings or signatures.
- Do not add filler introductions or conclusions.
- Keep the report professional, organized, and easy to search by subject.

